<title>JAPAN: RTRS-Japan December aluminium imports down 5.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Japan December aluminium imports down 5.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium imports fell to 211,553 tonnes in December, off 5.4 percent from 223,699 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry statistics released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Dec 96	    Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Total	  211,553	   233,013     223,699</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	  33,197	    50,374	60,799</p>
<p> Russia	  39,892	    28,648	31,586</p>
<p> Australia     26,477	    30,230	24,621</p>
<p> U.S.	    11,268	    14,950	19,078</p>
<p>Refined aluminium imports in 1996 were 2,758,853 tonnes, off 1.6 percent from 2,802,781 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
